Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||06-14-2000||11:37 AM||||Okay, well, I had a day to drive me new '88 Formula arround befor it went into the shop for a tune up and to get the exhaust leak fixed. So, now I have to start working on the stuff I can do. I knowticed the break were rather dificult to push down and seemed kinda weak. This car has been sitting for about 2 years, so I know I have to at least clean up the rotors, but that doesn't explain why it's so hard to push the peddle (I mean I almost literally had to stand on it) it was like the power brakes, weren't. Any ideas? or where could I track down a new power booster, or if need be calipers. I know calipers are rather expencive tho (mega bummer). Okay, on to the more minor stuff, the P-Seal (I beleive that's what it's called) on the T-Tops (the little 'felt' strip that kinda pads the glass from the roof). I've heard this is also a pretty expencive set to purchase, my question: can I just go down to K-Mart and pick up a few feet of velcro and use the fuzzy side? another small one, the manual mirror aiming device on the drivers side, the base of the plastic is coming loose from the door cloth, is there some kind of internal clip inside, and if so, what's the best way to get at it? Okay, well, I supose that'll do it for now, Thanks for any help or ideas!||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||06-14-2000||11:58 AM||||It's quite possible that you have a vacuum leak in the hose going to your beake booster or maybe the power booster itself is inoperative.<P>Also the caliper slider bolts probably need regreased with that special synthetic caliper bolt grease. The old grease, if there is any left, is probably all stiff and gunky.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Boxdin||06-14-2000||12:12 PM||||From my experience with my 3 Formulas, the brake fluid (and clutch fluid) must be changed ASAP. I have seen lots of corrosion inside these lines, along with the degredation of calipers, master & slave cyl. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||06-14-2000||12:36 PM||||Thanks for the tips guys, I figured it might be the vacuum hose, so that'll be my first check, and I'll change the brake fluid this weekend, and check the lines for anything out of the usual. Just from the small ammount I drove it tho it just seems like such a fun little car!||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||06-14-2000||01:00 PM||||Hey Rick, is it possible to lock any or all of your brakes?  I had an overly firm pedal in my 88 Coupe and the left front brake always locked way earlier than the right - turned out to be a stuck caliper on the right front.  The left rear turned out to be stuck too.  Excessive creaking from your brakes is another bad sign - possible stuck sliders.<P>Maybe you'll get lucky and it will just be the vacuum assist.||||reg||1
